ail.com> wrote:
The curly braces are quotes for Lojban text within text of other languages.=
 I'm not quite sure why they're used, but it's a kind of standard.
For upper case apostrophe, I'll give the example of the name of selma'o {KO=
hA} (again, braces are "quotes"). It is derrived from {ko'a}. So, as 'K' is=
 capital 'k', 'h' is capital apostrophe.
On Saturday, 24 November 2012 00:14:36 UTC, Annie wrote:
